Almost all grazing on broken hillsides; very few
flat lands. Almost all grazing, very few flat ground.



Description and notes:
Until 1980’s there was herding here. Now completely overgrown. Could accomodate 1000 sh. and goats. It had a roofed area. Animals stayed outside of the walled pen, on sides of hills.
500 m. S of this fold, at a higher hill is a singular shepherd’s hut. All animals sleep outside of it. Belongs to SÖ. 

* SD-2 is totally demolished. It is along Sögütlüdere. About 250 m to Avsar. accomodates c. 250 animals in roofed area. Not drawn.
** Sögütlüdere and Yatakdere are on each side of a valley bottom-- At Sögütlüdere there are 2 agıls at Yatakdere, there are 3.
Totally demolished..at ca. same elev. as SD-1, at 1,300 m. About 250 m. to Avsar.
Accomodates c. 250 animals in roofed area.

Sögütlüdere and Yatakdere are on each side of a valley-bottom. At Sögütlü there are 2 agıls; at Y. there are 3 agıls..






SD-1  at Hacı Tugrul,  Hacı Ismail Agılı: 
We went there with Satılmıs dede from Avsar village which has grazing land bordering it.
Local name: Sögütlüdere; Çile Mt. slopes- YAYLA
Location: Hacı Tugrul; Hacı Ismail agılı; at c. 1,300 m.
type: closed/dismantled
Land Use in Larger Area: almost all grazing; very little flat ground.
Topography: high, gentle, rolling hills-- almost devoid of trees or bushes. Fold on edge of the streambed (Sögütlü)..

Agıl: closed agıl proper is c. 50 sq.m. But the herds grazed and stayed outdoors, for 6 months in the hills above. So, estimated herd size in roofed area is c. 300 ; another 600-700 could have stayed in the open area.


Until ‘80’s there was herd here. Now, completely overgrown. Could accomodate 1,000 sheep and goats. It had a roofed area. Animals stayed outdoors of the walled pen, on hillside. After increase of herds, shepherd moved hut higher as herds slept outside on hillside.

SUMMER OPEN FOLD - 500 m. south of the fold, at a higher hill is a singular shepherd’s hut, with no fold. Animals sleep around it. Belongs to SÖ village, Cemal.

Satılmıs Dede as Shepherd: Pure Bosnian. started c. 55 years ago with 150 animals; increased it to 600. Grazing was very good, lots of flowers and much grass. Exclusively Karaman with fat sheep. Moved later to Merinos, but not as good. 
Had there been many herds, there wuld not be so much high grass and thorns..Herds would have stomped it. Nowadays, at this elev. we have oak trees. In the past we cut it down in large quantities, carrying it with donkey-carts.

	Summer Cycle: : When there were a lot of herds, we took them mostly to highland grazing and stayed there till Nov. A few animals remained in the village.
In Winter, came to village, with the first snow.

 AVSAR -
Streams are numerous at Avsar: Sögütlüdere, Pirayle, Kavakpınarı...

In our neighboring village, Karaahmet, there used to be 8,000-9,000 animals, in ‘50s to ‘60s. Though  there is so much grazingland there, very few animals. Same goes for SÖ. Economical conditions are very difficult.

The total land area is c. 2,600 d. About half is for grazing. But neighboring villages allow us to  graze our animals..we did not even give them rental...Müslim, Hacıtugrul, SÖ, Karaahmet etc.. 
Tiftik: We sold it to merchants: Polatlı, Ayas, Ankara, Beypazarı...Now state cooperatives buy it, but for little price and they waste it in storage..terrible.

Barley: We grow it to sell and as feed...after keeping enough for winter (10-15 tons) we sell the rest. 
Agriculture done with tractor.

We walked along Sögütlüdere (base of Çile Dag), came to Yatakdere.  Sögütlüdere and Yatakdere are on each side of a valley-bottom. At S. there are 2 agıls; at Y. there are 3 agıls.

